Synthetic test blocks import `test_b0_integrity.py`'s writers (`_trace`, `_router`, `_residency`, `_block`) and the module constants (EXPERTS=16, LAYERS=[19, 20], ...) rather than copying them. Scorer code takes `num_experts` as a parameter so those 16-expert fixtures work.

b1_rows.py:
- Constants: NUM_EXPERTS=384, GATE_DEPTH=12, TRAINED_HORIZONS=(1,2,4), SPLITS=('train','dev','calib','locked_test').
- Layout: `<D>/<split>/x/<session>.bin` (uint16 [N,5120]) and `<D>/<split>/h<h>/<session>.npz`.
- `class Group(msgspec.Struct, frozen=True)` with fields:
  - identity: session, split, block, seq:int, rid:str, warm_start:bool, flagged:bool;
  - source and target: horizon:int, source_row, source_layer, source_stratum:str, gate_has_bias:bool (the target row's), target_row, target_layer, target_stratum:str;
  - tokens: int16 [n], the kept live token indices;
  - x_offset:int, where the group's n x rows start in the session's x shard;
  - source_ids int16 [n,6], source_weights f32 [n,6], target_ids int16 [n,6], target_kinds uint8 [n,6];
  - ram_mask uint64 [6] (the target's 384-bit snapshot); hot int16 [k] (the target layer's VRAM-hot set);
  - gate_ids int16 [n,12] and gate_scores f32 [n,12]: the target gate on x[T], biased, best first; -1/-inf when the target has no biased gate.
- `eligible(g) -> np.ndarray[int16]`: unique experts routed with kind MISS_GPU or MISS_CPU over kept tokens.
- `never_candidates(g) -> np.ndarray`: eligible experts outside gate_ids of every token.
- `in_ram(g, experts) -> bool array`.
- `write_groups(out_dir, *, split, horizon, session, groups)` and `write_x(out_dir, *, split, session, x)`.
- `read_groups(dataset_dir, *, split, horizon, sessions=None, frozen_sha256=None) -> Iterator[Group]`: session then seq order; raises PermissionError for split=='locked_test' when frozen_sha256 is None.
- `read_x(dataset_dir, *, split, session, frozen_sha256=None) -> np.memmap uint16` (same refusal).
- `x_rows(xmap, g) -> f32 [n,5120]`.
- `class TokenScores(msgspec.Struct, frozen=True)`: scores f32 [n, E] (-inf = no candidate), rule: Literal['margin','noisy_or','count'], floor: float|None=None.
- `class Scorer(Protocol)`: name: str; `__call__(g: Group) -> TokenScores`.

